<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring maps Schnakenberg, k_c, the 96 µm predecessor, and the Galerkin card fit to Turing, Gierer-Meinhardt, and Yamaguchi. Lean theorems are integer witnesses of the same identities, not a real-analysis formalization of σ(k)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the Schnakenberg Jacobian, σ(k), and a calibration that puts the maximum-growth wavelength at 41.016 µm. The rendered carrier for that wavelength is then placed with an inverted scale factor, so the picture is not yet the 41 µm mode." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9923 and radial Pearson r = 0.9997, with RMSE 0.669 gray levels and KS D = 0.0265. The reported dark-ring pitch is 82.14 µm because measure_scale_bar returns µm/px (0.9009) and segment_card divides by it. The 41 µm mode power fraction is 0.0014. KS p-value is computed and dropped." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py L191–L208: scale bar returns 100/width <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L191-L208>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ablation-growth-rate-at-41-m-when-du-dv>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ancestral-96-m-mode-growth-rate>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-analytic-vs-numeric-growth-rate-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ocellus-card-radial-profile-galerkin-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ocellus-card-radial-profile-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-selected-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-ocellus-dominant-dark-ring-pitch>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-ocellus-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-ocellus-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-radial-profile-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 82.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg linear dispersion is calibrated so argmax σ(k) = 41.016 µm at age 0 Ma (Du = 10.659 µm², Dv = 191.861 µm², ratio 18). Analytic versus numeric growth-rate Pearson r = 0.9923 (RMSE 0.051). The axisymmetric Galerkin fit to the ocellus card has Pearson r = 0.9997. The scale helper returns 100/width (µm per px, 0.9009) but callers treat it as px per µm, so the 41 µm carrier carries only 0.14% of the wave amplitude and the dark-ring pitch is reported as 82.14 µm instead of about 67 µm. σ(96 µm) = -0.490 (mandarina contrast damped) and the Du = Dv ablation growth rate is -1.315. Overall 82.5/100 (faithfulness 80.7, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3132697 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 d768ef9b85c6ae76a7f674e668a292fc07b7b7d90eccba040817d9e558195de4 (sha256 d768ef9b85c6ae76a7f674e668a292fc07b7b7d90eccba040817d9e558195de4), spec_fingerprint 900e8c4cd551803050526b60486b8aa4c0338d7c662a7b9812395080ca4e0324. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 900e8c4cd551803050526b60486b8aa4c0338d7c662a7b9812395080ca4e0324; artifact_sha256: d768ef9b85c6ae76a7f674e668a292fc07b7b7d90eccba040817d9e558195de4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_adult_cc0.jpg=76144516fb810472..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_ocellus_specimen.jpg=2adf51228d2da684..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0a11d56294fb484c..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=08ab9cb9580075e6..., datasets/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=9e4a322221a85be7...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yamaguchi et al. 2013: periodic Wnt1 expression generates Bombyx larval twin spots. | Turing 1952 and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: a finite wavelength is selected when the inhibitor diffuses farther than the activator.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian with a = 0.058, b = 0.94, Dv/Du = 18, rescaled so λ_c = 41 µm. | Axisymmetric Galerkin sideband fitted to the canonical ocellus card. | Predecessor contrast σ(2π/96 µm) < 0 < σ(2π/41 µm) at 0 Ma. No successor chronospecies.; transfer_boundary: Wnt1 twin spots in the source paper are segment-scale. The 41 µm figure is this slot's cellular detail scale, not a length Yamaguchi measured.; does_not_claim: That 41 µm or 96 µm was measured on a fossil or on Bombyx mandarina. | That the Pass-1 ring pitch of 82.14 µm is the card's true pitch. The unit conversion is inverted. | A pixel-fitted nonlinear 2D spot field.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'measure_scale_bar returns micrometres per pixel (100/width) while fit_galerkin and segment_card treat the value as pixels per micrometre. Return width/100, re-place the 41 µm carrier, and recompute the dark-ring pitch.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Replace the constant-gray ablation panel with a field evolved at Du = Dv from the same seeded noise, and keep the numeric growth rate σ < 0.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Emit the Kolmogorov-Smirnov p-value as its own measurement (value not equal to the reference) alongside D, Pearson r, and RMSE.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Re-render the GIF after the scale correction and re-score computer-vision similarity against the ocellus card.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.25e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
