<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Bombyx mori)",
        "Bombyx mori Turing wavenumber selection at 41 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Bombyx mori morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bombyx mori specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Bombyx mori" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A pixel-fitted nonlinear 2D spot field.",
        "does_not_claim: That 41 µm or 96 µm was measured on a fossil or on Bombyx mandarina.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Pass-1 ring pitch of 82.14 µm is the card's true pitch. The unit conversion is inverted.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Axisymmetric Galerkin sideband fitted to the canonical ocellus card.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Predecessor contrast σ(2π/96 µm) < 0 < σ(2π/41 µm) at 0 Ma. No successor chronospecies.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian with a = 0.058, b = 0.94, Dv/Du = 18, rescaled so λ_c = 41 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: a finite wavelength is selected when the inhibitor diffuses farther than the activator.",
        "reported_in_source: Yamaguchi et al. 2013: periodic Wnt1 expression generates Bombyx larval twin spots.",
        "transfer_boundary: Wnt1 twin spots in the source paper are segment-scale. The 41 µm figure is this slot's cellular detail scale, not a length Yamaguchi measured." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Bombyx mori" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Bombyx" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; output: docs/media/bombyx_mori_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Bombyx mori; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Yamaguchi et al. 2013: periodic Wnt1 expression generates Bombyx larval twin spots. | Turing 1952 and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972: a finite wavelength is selected when the inhibitor diffuses farther than the activator.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian with a = 0.058, b = 0.94, Dv/Du = 18, rescaled so λ_c = 41 µm. | Axisymmetric Galerkin sideband fitted to the canonical ocellus card. | Predecessor contrast σ(2π/96 µm) < 0 < σ(2π/41 µm) at 0 Ma. No successor chronospecies.; transfer_boundary: Wnt1 twin spots in the source paper are segment-scale. The 41 µm figure is this slot's cellular detail scale, not a length Yamaguchi measured.; does_not_claim: That 41 µm or 96 µm was measured on a fossil or on Bombyx mandarina. | That the Pass-1 ring pitch of 82.14 µm is the card's true pitch. The unit conversion is inverted. | A pixel-fitted nonlinear 2D spot field.]; phenomenon_size: 32 µm (3.2e-05 m, log10=-4.495 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 32 µm to 9.2 cm): 32 µm:bombyx-mori-bioelectric-polarity, 114 µm:bombyx-mori-vertex-packing, 2.0 mm:bombyx-mori-turing-wavelength, 3.9 mm:bombyx-mori-clock-wavefront, 6.7 mm:bombyx-mori-morphogen-condensation, 8.6 mm:bombyx-mori-flux-canalization, 9.4 mm:bombyx-mori-elastic-buckling, 1.1 cm:bombyx-mori-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
